        <h1>LeetCode 2913: Subarrays Distinct Element Sum of Squares I (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a 0-indexed integer array nums. The distinct count of a subarray of nums is
                defined as the number of distinct values present in that subarray. Return the sum of the
                squares of the distinct counts of all subarrays of nums. A subarray is a contiguous non-empty
                sequence of elements within an array.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [1,2,1]<br>
                Output: 15<br>
                Explanation: The six subarrays are [1], [2], [1], [1,2], [2,1], and [1,2,1]. Their distinct
                counts are 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, and 2, so the sum of squares is 1 + 1 + 1 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 15.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int sumCounts(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
        int n = nums.size(), ans = 0;
        for (int start = 0; start &lt; n; start++) {
            bitset&lt;101&gt; vis;
            for (int end = start; end &lt; n; end++) {
                vis.set(nums[end]);
                int distinct = vis.count();
                ans += distinct * distinct;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
};</code></pre>
